Yes, that's expected. The title of this issue is quite literally just the expected behavior of the code cited initially:
```c
  LOOP_PROCESS_EVENTS_UNTIL(tui->loop, tui->loop->events, EXIT_TIMEOUT_MS,
                            tui->stopped || tui->input.read_stream.did_eof);
  if (!tui->stopped && !tui->input.read_stream.did_eof) {
    WLOG("TUI: timed out waiting for DA1 response");
  }
```
But we block there for good reason, and it works fine in a well-behaved terminal.
